<section class="sheet" id="read"><div class="section-kicker">Document 09 · standalone working plan</div><h2>How to read this roadmap</h2><p class="lede">This document gives the sequence, evidence and approval gates for delivering the proposed Unified Product Catalogue to Search, Recommendations and Campaigns Data Science. Waves are gated outcomes, not calendar promises. Work may overlap where it does not bypass a gate.</p><div class="callout warn"><strong>Planning status.</strong> The source route, canonical Article ID, actual first-release attribute list, source authority, history and service targets are not approved. The later five-wave roadmap is used here because it states the gates more clearly. An earlier seven-phase plan included indicative weeks and months; those ranges are not committed dates and are not silently carried into this plan.</div><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Label</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span class="status-tag confirmed">Current evidence</span></td><td>A fact or observed gap supported by the supplied source material.</td></tr><tr><td><span class="status-tag proposed">Working gate</span></td><td>Recommended sequencing, control or evidence requirement pending the accountable owner’s approval.</td></tr><tr><td><span class="status-tag open">Open</span></td><td>A decision, threshold, owner or target that cannot be assumed from the source documents.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="sheet" id="scope"><div class="section-kicker">Programme boundary</div><h2>What is being delivered</h2><p>Today the squads use different product-data feeds, joins and snapshots. SAP/PLM and STEP PIM author different product concepts; BEAM has distinct master-data, PIM attribute and Navigation paths. The target is a governed analytical product in BEAM’s Data Science Optimized (DSO) boundary. Private adapters resolve identities and source differences; accepted, versioned outputs become the shared Data Science surface. The source route is conditional on ADR-01.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Proposed primary output</th><th>Business grain and use</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>product_article_current</code></td><td>Article × market × channel; current identity and stable descriptive fields.</td></tr><tr><td><code>product_sku_current</code></td><td>SKU × market × channel; SKU identity and Article relationship.</td></tr><tr><td><code>product_attribute_current</code></td><td>Entity × market × channel × attribute; governed broader attribute inventory.</td></tr><tr><td><code>product_navigation_current</code></td><td>Article × category × hierarchy/version × market × channel × validity; online navigation membership.</td></tr><tr><td><code>product_attribute_history</code></td><td>Entity × market × channel × attribute × effective interval; point-in-time descriptive history.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The supporting identifier crosswalk preserves raw-to-canonical mappings over time. Price, Stock/Availability, Promotions and Reviews are separately owned related-domain proposals. MongoDB, PostgreSQL and Elasticsearch continue operational or real-time serving in the current scope; this plan concerns duplicated <em>analytical</em> use.</p></section>
