<tr><td>0 · Mobilise and approve route</td><td>Name owners, obtain source access, agree comparison rules and establish the private DSO boundary.</td><td>ADR-01 route decision; source contacts; data classification/access path; decision cadence and working scope.</td><td>BEAM Architecture/Governance; Product Owner; Data Governance.</td></tr>
<tr><td>1 · Discover and reconcile</td><td>Confirm the actual minimum attributes and their location; inventory broader fields; align a comparable dataset to the Recommendations snapshot.</td><td>Article-ID collision/coverage profiling; grain, market and business-time alignment; source metadata; field differences classified and owned.</td><td>Architecture, source/domain owners and Data Science leads.</td></tr>
<tr><td>2 · Publish MVP contracts</td><td>Build and expose all five primary contracts at the approved initial scope.</td><td>Schema, quality, lineage, security, history and consumer-parity checks passed; monitoring, recovery and support active.</td><td>Product Owner, Design Authority, BEAM Engineering and squad leads.</td></tr>
<tr><td>3 · Migrate consumers</td><td>Move approved squad analytical reads through parallel validation and a reversible cutover.</td><td>Per-squad tolerance and sign-off; observation window; rollback and support handover; dependent analytical consumers identified.</td><td>Each squad lead and BEAM operational owner.</td></tr>
<tr><td>4 · Strategic expansion</td><td>Onboard the governed wider attribute inventory and approved related domains through repeatable change control.</td><td>Attribute/domain owner decisions, onboarding SLA, quality and schema-evolution controls, and adoption evidence for each release.</td><td>Product Owner, domain owners, Data Governance and Design Authority.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div><p class="meta">This sequence does not preclude preparation for later waves during earlier work. If an MVP contract lacks attributes needed for a squad use case, that use case stays on its legacy analytical path until expansion closes the gap and parity passes. Wave 3 and Wave 4 work may overlap; neither permits retiring an unmet dependency.</p></section>
<section class="sheet" id="mvp"><div class="section-kicker">Wave 2 acceptance</div><h2>Minimum evidence before calling the MVP complete</h2><div class="table-scroll"><table class="checklist"><thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>Evidence to present</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Actual attribute slate</td><td>A named, agreed list of the minimum attributes with definition, grain, owner, authority, source path, type, unit, sensitivity, quality rule and disposition. The illustrative “22” template is not approval.</td></tr><tr><td>Five primary contracts</td><td>Each exists at its declared grain with explicit market/channel scope and signed field/schema version.</td></tr><tr><td>Identifier resolution</td><td>Raw values, identifier type, source, scope, validity and derivation rule retained. Competing Article-ID derivations profiled for uniqueness, collisions, stability, coverage and traceability.</td></tr><tr><td>Comparable reconciliation</td><td>Population, market, grain, business time, null semantics and units aligned before comparing values; mismatches classified and accepted or assigned.</td></tr><tr><td>Navigation</td><td>Approved Navigation-domain path and completeness; buying hierarchy is not substituted for online category membership.</td></tr><tr><td>History</td><td>Current and history reconcile at the agreed cut-off; late arrivals and restatements visible; selected past business date can be reconstructed.</td></tr><tr><td>Consumer proof</td><td>Representative Search, Recommendations and Campaigns use cases run in parallel with agreed tolerances and recorded exceptions.</td></tr><tr><td>Operational readiness</td><td>Quality gates, access controls, monitoring, recovery runbook, support routing and rollback path demonstrated.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="callout alert"><strong>Hold the gate if a core decision is unresolved.</strong> Article ID, source authority, market/channel scope, the real MVP attribute list and retention/restatement policy must be resolved or explicitly bounded before an approved production contract is claimed.</div></section>
