rtant" class="nodeLabel"><p>5 · Cut over analytical reads; retain rollback</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g><g class="node default decision" id="upc-09-consumer-cutover-flowchart-O-14" data-look="classic" transform="translate(607.2265625, 1235)"><polygon points="163,0 326,-163 163,-326 0,-163" class="label-container" transform="translate(-162.5, 163)" style="fill:#fff5df !important;stroke:#9a6100 !important"/><g class="label" style="color:#172231 !important" transform="translate(-100, -48)"><rect/><foreignObject width="200" height="96"><div style="color: rgb(23, 34, 49) !important; display: table; white-space: break-spaces; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 200px; text-align: center; width: 200px;" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><span style="color:#172231 !important" class="nodeLabel"><p>6 · Observation window stable<br />and downstream dependents migrated?</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g><g class="node default issue" id="upc-09-consumer-cutover-flowchart-R-16" data-look="classic" transform="translate(317.33203125, 1511)"><rect class="basic label-container" style="fill:#fff0ed !important;stroke:#a43c39 !important" x="-130" y="-39" width="260" height="78"/><g class="label" style="color:#172231 !important" transform="translate(-100, -24)"><rect/><foreignObject width="200" height="48"><div style="color: rgb(23, 34, 49) !important; display: table; white-space: break-spaces; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 200px; text-align: center; width: 200px;" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><span style="color:#172231 !important" class="nodeLabel"><p>Rollback or repair; keep legacy analytical path</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g><g class="node default done" id="upc-09-consumer-cutover-flowchart-Z-19" data-look="classic" transform="translate(627.33203125, 1511)"><rect class="basic label-container" style="fill:#ddf2e8 !important;stroke:#17744f !important" x="-130" y="-39" width="260" height="78"/><g class="label" style="color:#172231 !important" transform="translate(-100, -24)"><rect/><foreignObject width="200" height="48"><div style="color: rgb(23, 34, 49) !important; display: table; white-space: break-spaces; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 200px; text-align: center; width: 200px;" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><span style="color:#172231 !important" class="nodeLabel"><p>7 · Retire only redundant analytical artefact</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g></g></g></g><defs><filter id="upc-09-consumer-cutover-drop-shadow" height="130%" width="130%"><feDropShadow dx="4" dy="4" stdDeviation="0" flood-opacity="0.06" flood-color="#000000"/></filter></defs><defs><filter id="upc-09-consumer-cutover-drop-shadow-small" height="150%" width="150%"><feDropShadow dx="2" dy="2" stdDeviation="0" flood-opacity="0.06" flood-color="#000000"/></filter></defs></svg></div></div><p class="diagram-caption">A parity failure loops back to investigation and a fresh parallel run. Cutover remains reversible until the agreed observation and downstream-dependency checks pass.</p><details><summary>Editable Mermaid source</summary><pre class="source-code">flowchart TB
  B[&quot;1 · Freeze reproducible legacy baseline&quot;] --&gt; P[&quot;2 · Run legacy and new contract in parallel&quot;]
  P --&gt; C[&quot;3 · Compare IDs, coverage, values, freshness and model outputs;&lt;br/&gt;classify differences&quot;]
